notes.body:
I took a look at the Quake dissectors.

It seems like Quake1 and 2 just do a `dissector_add_uint_with_preference("udp.port", DEFAULTnet_hostport, quake_handle);` while Quake3 does some slightly weirder
```c
	if (!initialized) {
		quake3_handle = create_dissector_handle(dissect_quake3,
				proto_quake3);
		initialized=TRUE;
	} else {
		for (i=0;i<4;i++)
			dissector_delete_uint("udp.port", server_port+i, quake3_handle);
		for (i=0;i<4;i++)
			dissector_delete_uint("udp.port", master_port+i, quake3_handle);
	}

	/* set port for future deletes */
	server_port = gbl_quake3_server_port;
	master_port = gbl_quake3_master_port;

	/* add dissectors. Port preference names to specific to use "auto" */
	for (i=0;i<4;i++)
		dissector_add_uint("udp.port", gbl_quake3_server_port + i,
			quake3_handle);
	for (i=0;i<4;i++)
		dissector_add_uint("udp.port", gbl_quake3_master_port + i,
			quake3_handle);

```

I have resorted to `dissector_add_for_decode_as` as mentioned by @guyharris since it seems to be the wisest option when the dissector just blindly accepts everything as it currently does.
